WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.060
<v Instructor>So now let's talk about Amazon ECR.</v>

2
00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.940
So the Elastic Container Registry is used to store

3
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.000
and manage Docker images on AWS.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.890
And you have two kind of repositories,

5
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.310
you have the Private and the Public repositories.

6
00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.200
By the way, there is a whole repository you

7
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.990
can see called gallery.ecr.aws,

8
00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.510
it has public images you can get.

9
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.790
So you have an ECR repository, and for example,

10
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.670
you have two Docker images, A and B

11
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.710
and then you have an ECS cluster.

12
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.140
And the Instance is going to have a role

13
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.800
that allows it to pull images from the ECR repository

14
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.380
and therefore start containers on it.

15
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.560
So the ECR is fully integrated ECS

16
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.560
in terms of pulling Docker images

17
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.530
and the access to ECR is controlled through IAM.

18
00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.270
So in case you have any permission errors,

19
00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.790
you need to check the policies.

20
00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.700
Now, ECR has many features. We'll see those in a bit.

21
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.550
We have vulnerability scanning, versioning,

22
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.160
image tags, image lifecycle, and so on.

23
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.720
So some features you must know, for example,

24
00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.940
is the cross-Region replication.

25
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.800
So it both supports cross-Region

26
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.020
and cross-account replication in ECR.

27
00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:07.950
So let's take an example.

28
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:12.024
Say you have a pipeline to build images from CodeBuild.

29
00:01:12.024 --> 00:01:14.760
So CodeBuild will run container, will build images

30
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:19.050
and will register and push these images to Amazon ECR.

31
00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.590
Then from ECR, if you've set up cross-Region replication

32
00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:25.230
these images are going to be replicated directly

33
00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.940
into other regions.

34
00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.760
The advantage that you don't have to rebuild these images

35
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.110
into other regions

36
00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.380
and you can start launching, for example, your task on ECS

37
00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.163
from other regions as well, giving you a global application.

38
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.240
Another feature is the image scanning.

39
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.430
So Amazon ECR creates containers

40
00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.980
and it's important to scan these containers

41
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.500
to look for vulnerabilities.

42
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.840
So they can be either manual scan

43
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.120
or automatic scan with scan on push.

44
00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.140
So whenever you push an image into your ECR repository

45
00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.150
then the image is going to be scanned.

46
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.380
Now you have two types of scan.

47
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.660
You have the basic scanning that looks

48
00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.120
for common vulnerability.

49
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.310
So we push an image into ECR.

50
00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:12.570
ECR is going to scan the image through its service itself

51
00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.550
and then the results in case, for example,

52
00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.320
you have vulnerabilities.

53
00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.430
They can be triggered

54
00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:20.670
and sent as events into EventBridge.

55
00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.290
That's for the basic scanning.

56
00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.240
And then you have enhanced scanning,

57
00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:27.210
and that actually leverages the Amazon Inspector Service,

58
00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.860
and it's going to do more than just looking

59
00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:31.050
for common CVE is going to look

60
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.500
for operating system and programming language vulnerability.

61
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.050
So it's a deeper scan, it's enhanced scanning.

62
00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.390
So again, we push an image into ECR

63
00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.940
but this time the inspector service is going

64
00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.500
to scan our image.

65
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.830
And then in case we have any results of that scan,

66
00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.660
it's going to be in EventBridge.

67
00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.780
But this time the trigger service is inspector,

68
00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.430
it's not ECR.

69
00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.860
Also, you can view the scan results directly

70
00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:00.480
from the AWS console for both types of scanning.

71
00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.730
Okay, so that's it for Amazon ECR.

72
00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.680
I hope you liked it and I will see you in the next lecture.

